It is Saturday morning at seven o'clock.
I am still sleeping heavily.
Suddenly I feel something cold on my arm.
I open my eyes and see Ludwig.
He nudges me with his snout.
"Good morning, Ludwig," I say and get up.
We go out into the kitchen together.
He is very hungry and jumps up on me.
"Easy now, Ludwig," I say to him.
"Sit," I say calmly.
He looks at me and sits down on the floor.
I take the bag of dog food and open it.
I pour the food into his bowl.
He gets up because he wants it immediately.
"No, wait," I say.
He sits down again and waits nicely.
I put the bowl down in front of him.
I gently pet him on the head.
"Here you go, eat," I say with a smile.
He wags his tail and begins to eat.
